 ## API
 
-- `parse(text)`: milliseconds from a duration made of `h`, `m`, `s` and `ms`
-  parts. Throws `TypeError` on empty input and `SyntaxError` on anything else
-  it cannot read.
-- `format(ms)`: the largest units first, separated by spaces. `0` is `"0s"`.
+- `parse(text)`: milliseconds from a duration made of `d`, `h`, `m`, `s` and
+  `ms` parts. Throws `TypeError` on empty input and `SyntaxError` on anything
+  else it cannot read.
+- `format(ms, options?)`: the largest units first, separated by spaces. `0` is
+  `"0s"`. Days are shown only with `{ days: true }`, so `format(90000000)` is
+  `"25h"` and `format(90000000, { days: true })` is `"1d 1h"`.
 
 ## Versioning
 
